# Backend Design Curriculum (Developer to Principal)

This repository is a structured study guide that takes a developer from
fundamentals to principal-level backend design. It covers core CS, system
design, operations, security, and leadership practices.

## Progression guide
- Beginner: learn fundamentals and build small services.
- Intermediate: design complete APIs, data models, and deployments.
- Senior: make tradeoffs across performance, reliability, and cost.
- Principal: set org standards, lead architecture, and drive alignment.

## How to use this curriculum
- Start at module 1; experienced developers can skip ahead.
- Each module README lists topics and progression expectations.
- For each module, produce artifacts such as:
  - Architecture/design docs and ADRs.
  - Operational runbooks and SLO/SLI definitions.
  - Performance budgets and scalability plans.
  - Security threat models and data governance notes.
- Revisit modules at deeper levels as you advance.

## Outcomes
- Build backend services with strong foundations.
- Design scalable systems and justify tradeoffs.
- Operate services reliably, securely, and cost-effectively.
- Lead technical direction across teams.

## Modules
1. [Foundations and Programming Basics](01-foundations-and-programming-basics/)
   - Master fundamentals and establish coding practices and tooling.
2. [Data Structures and Algorithms](02-data-structures-and-algorithms/)
   - Apply algorithmic tradeoffs to real systems.
3. [Computer Systems and OS](03-computer-systems-and-os/)
   - Understand runtime behavior, resource limits, and performance.
4. [Networking and HTTP](04-networking-and-http/)
   - Design reliable, secure network interactions.
5. [Databases and Data Modeling](05-databases-and-data-modeling/)
   - Plan scalable data architectures and governance.
6. [API Design and Contracts](06-api-design-and-contracts/)
   - Build durable APIs with clear versioning and compatibility.
7. [Backend Architecture and Patterns](07-backend-architecture-and-patterns/)
   - Define system boundaries, patterns, and reference architectures.
8. [Frameworks and Tech Stack](08-frameworks-and-tech-stack/)
   - Select technology stacks and tooling for long-term health.
9. [Security and Authentication](09-security-and-authentication/)
   - Establish security practices and risk management.
10. [Caching and Performance](10-caching-and-performance/)
    - Meet performance goals with optimization techniques.
11. [Distributed Systems and System Design](11-distributed-systems-and-system-design/)
    - Design scalable systems with clear consistency tradeoffs.
12. [Messaging and Event-Driven](12-messaging-and-event-driven/)
    - Build reliable async systems with strong contracts.
13. [DevOps and CI/CD](13-devops-and-ci-cd/)
    - Create safe, automated delivery pipelines.
14. [Observability and Monitoring](14-observability-and-monitoring/)
    - Define SLOs, signals, and actionable alerting.
15. [Testing and Quality](15-testing-and-quality/)
    - Drive quality and test strategy.
16. [Reliability and SRE](16-reliability-and-sre/)
    - Align reliability goals with operational practice.
17. [Cloud and Deployment](17-cloud-and-deployment/)
    - Deploy secure, scalable systems with cost control.
18. [Capstone Case Studies](18-capstone-case-studies/)
    - Practice end-to-end design and tradeoff analysis.